1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,669
Notary. No certificate, no money moves.

2
00:00:04,136 --> 00:00:08,884
AI agents are starting to move real money:
refunds, plan changes, credits.

3
00:00:08,989 --> 00:00:10,963
They learn how from API docs.

4
00:00:11,381 --> 00:00:14,283
But docs and real APIs disagree.

5
00:00:14,956 --> 00:00:20,112
We pointed our agent at two real APIs,
Crustdata and Dodo Payments.

6
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:25,023
Crustdata's own docs say a company lookup
with no match returns an empty result.

7
00:00:25,534 --> 00:00:30,642
In our run, it returned an error instead,
and three documented claims didn't hold.

8
00:00:30,886 --> 00:00:34,926
An agent that trusts the docs breaks on
exactly these cases.

9
00:00:35,387 --> 00:00:39,509
Notary won't touch money until it has
proven how its tools behave.

10
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:42,829
It turns every promise in the docs into a
claim,

11
00:00:43,212 --> 00:00:46,184
commits a hashed prediction before each
test call,

12
00:00:46,393 --> 00:00:49,110
then calls the API and compares.

13
00:00:49,923 --> 00:00:54,950
A Reflector proposes explanations, and a
stronger Adversary tries to refute them.

14
00:00:55,647 --> 00:00:58,955
In our runs, it narrowed all five beliefs.

15
00:00:59,338 --> 00:01:01,533
What survives becomes a certificate.

16
00:01:01,974 --> 00:01:07,326
No certificate, no money moves: the Guard
holds anything uncovered for a person to

17
00:01:07,407 --> 00:01:08,405
review.

18
00:01:08,858 --> 00:01:12,689
neatlogs is how we looked into these
incidents and checked how each one was

19
00:01:12,747 --> 00:01:13,421
resolved.

20
00:01:13,862 --> 00:01:18,866
Each run is one trace, with every probe
and model call behind it.

21
00:01:19,377 --> 00:01:23,927
On the Crustdata run, the trace showed a
disputed claim's prediction,

22
00:01:24,252 --> 00:01:28,548
logged with its hash before the call, and
an inconclusive result.

23
00:01:28,989 --> 00:01:33,297
So Notary abstained, and no payment can
depend on that claim.

24
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:38,927
Two more mismatches stay open and
uncertified, so the Guard blocks them.

25
00:01:39,624 --> 00:01:44,233
On the Dodo run, the trace showed the
Adversary narrowing four beliefs,

26
00:01:44,407 --> 00:01:47,576
like wallet credits in minor units only
for US dollars,

27
00:01:47,855 --> 00:01:51,210
so Notary certified only that narrower
scope.

28
00:01:51,681 --> 00:01:54,107
Entire captured how Notary was built.

29
00:01:54,491 --> 00:01:58,937
Seven checkpoints tie each commit to the
coding-agent session that wrote it.

30
00:01:59,378 --> 00:02:04,313
Notary also uses Entire's code graph to
prove a safety property:

31
00:02:04,754 --> 00:02:08,051
every call that can move money goes
through a guard.

32
00:02:08,376 --> 00:02:10,768
Zero unguarded call sites.

33
00:02:11,229 --> 00:02:13,714
cfo.ai runs the business side.

34
00:02:14,143 --> 00:02:19,089
Notary measures what certainty costs,
about three cents of model spend and

35
00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:25,567
fifteen Crustdata credits per run, exports
those real costs to cfo.ai as a data

36
00:02:25,613 --> 00:02:31,302
source, and connects to cfo.ai's MCP
server to sync the plan back.

37
00:02:31,511 --> 00:02:34,449
And it's built to deploy on AWS.

38
00:02:34,904 --> 00:02:39,827
On our test suite, the agent without
Notary made nine unsafe money moves.

39
00:02:40,105 --> 00:02:44,099
With Notary, zero, and nine refunds held
for review.

40
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:48,325
Notary. No certificate, no money moves.
